cdk: free the cursor caches before the display's connection closes

The current cursor cache and the default arrow are held in qdata on the
display, and GObject clears the qdata at the end of the finalize stage,
after the class finalize chain has run: by then
cdk_x11_display_finalize has already called XCloseDisplay and freed the
Display, so their destroy notifies calling XFreeCursor ran on freed
memory whenever the display object was destroyed after a grab had
frozen a cursor.  The pre-existing cursor cache list avoids this by
being released from _cdk_x11_cursor_display_finalize, which runs before
XCloseDisplay.

Release both qdata there too, like the list, so the X cursor resources
are freed while the connection is still open on every teardown path,
and the destroy notifies only remain as a safety net.
